/* THE MIGRATION ARTIFACT — for an EXISTING repo adopting this standard. Not a second gate.
 *
 * Read this first, because otherwise the file looks redundant:
 *
 *   - In THIS starter (greenfield) `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` is already a hard gate in
 *     `tsconfig.app.json`. A new repo has no debt, so the flag costs nothing at commit one and
 *     every violation is caught as it is written. Here this file is a no-op that reports 0 errors,
 *     and the CI ratchet below is consequently already a hard gate. That is the intended end state.
 *
 *   - In an EXISTING repo the flag measures 906 errors across 193 files, and a rule set that lands
 *     hundreds of errors at once is the rule set that gets switched back off. So such a repo REMOVES
 *     `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` from `tsconfig.app.json`, leaves it enabled only here, and drives
 *     the count down directory by directory under the `typecheck-strict-ratchet` job in
 *     .github/workflows/ci.yml. When the count reaches 0, the flag moves into `tsconfig.app.json`
 *     and this file — with its baseline and its CI job — is deleted.
 *
 * So exactly one of the two spellings is live in any given repo. If you are editing this file
 * because it "does nothing", you are in a greenfield repo and the answer is to delete nothing.
 *
 * This IS a leaf config: it inherits `include: ["src"]` through `extends`, so it compiles real
 * files. Do not restate the flag in the root `tsconfig.json` — see the warning there.
 *
 * Not listed in the root config's `references`, so `tsc -b` never picks it up. It is run explicitly:
 *   tsc -p tsconfig.strict.json --noEmit
 */
{
    "extends": "./tsconfig.app.json",
    "compilerOptions": {
        /* Its own build-info path. Sharing tsconfig.app.json's would let a ratchet run and a
         * `npm run typecheck` run invalidate each other's cache under a different flag set. */
        "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.strict.tsbuildinfo",

        /* The one flag this config exists for. Inherited from tsconfig.app.json in a greenfield repo;
         * restated here so the file is self-contained after an existing repo removes it from there. */
        "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true
    }
}
